# Tern: Read Docs First

Before writing any code, read in order:
1. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system structure, two-phase model, data schemas
2. `docs/SCORING.md` — five axes, code generation, distinction logic
3. `docs/DESIGN.md` — visual system, screen states, animation specs
4. `AGENTS.md` — patterns and gotchas from prior sessions

If modifying questions, depth graph, or follow-up logic: also read `docs/QUESTIONS.md`.
For any visual, UI, map, character or animation work: read `docs/DESIGN.md` §0 and `prototypes/PLAN.md`. The experience direction (map, portrait, unlocks, worlds) is `docs/PLAN-progression.md`.

**Doc sync (non-negotiable):**
- Scoring/axis/convergence/distinction changes → update `docs/SCORING.md` before merging.
- Question wording, nudges, or triggers → update `docs/QUESTIONS.md`.
- Visual or animation changes → update `docs/DESIGN.md` first.
- After every session → append learnings to `AGENTS.md`.

No routing. State-driven rendering only. No backend in V1.
